{
  "obligations": [
    {
      "text": "Everything is measured and recorded in centimeters — no inches anywhere in the live protocol or the log.",
      "source_ids": ["msg-03"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Log entries are never deleted; if an entry is wrong, mark it VOID with a one-line reason and leave it in place.",
      "source_ids": ["msg-03"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Every alteration ID starts with the prefix GAV followed by a four-digit sequence number, so GAV-0001, GAV-0002 and so on.",
      "source_ids": ["msg-03"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Write for our volunteer stitchers — plain language, and any tailoring term of art gets a one-line gloss the first time it appears in a section.",
      "source_ids": ["msg-03"]
    },
    {
      "text": "This protocol is for 'The Glass Aviary' only. Harborside's other fall show, 'Rope Ladder,' keeps its own tracker, and I don't want our document drifting into a company template.",
      "source_ids": ["msg-05"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anything due within 48 hours of a performance is a rush item — tag it RUSH in the status line and float it to the top of the daily pull list.",
      "source_ids": ["msg-05"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Any alteration estimated over $150 in materials or labor goes in as PENDING-PM and can only be marked APPROVED once Ines Duarte, our production manager, initials it. At or under $150, Devon Okafor, my first hand, or I can approve directly.",
      "source_ids": ["msg-05"]
    },
    {
      "text": "For quick-change pieces — changes timed under 30 seconds — require two sets of initials at completion, one from the stitcher and one from the dresser.",
      "source_ids": ["msg-06"]
    },
    {
      "text": "When a rental ships back, move its entries to a separate rental archive sheet and strike them from the active log.",
      "source_ids": ["msg-07"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A rental can never be marked APPROVED for a permanent alteration unless a scanned owner-permission note is attached to the entry.",
      "source_ids": ["msg-07"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Capture the wearer's measurements on the entry — bust, waist, and hip in centimeters, taken at the time the alteration is logged.",
      "source_ids": ["msg-09"]
    }
  ]
}

